guamp: the whole reason of a refused texture to the kernel, and one retry after letting held imports go (Maps, fin40b)

fin40b (live-20261103-195840, 22:04 boot): Maps still aborts ("VectorKit received null texture from Metal"); 0011's lines show the
descriptor, "texref a f10 t2 u1 s0 1024x1024 m1 n1" and the same for the fallback: an ordinary R8Unorm 2D shared 1024x1024 texture,
refused as asked and with the usages trimmed, after "texture over buffer refused" in the same process; the surface refusals read
"Invalid(Invalid { ca..." cut at 46 characters. So not a format: the reason is needed.
- sendWhy: the reason of each refusal (texture "texwhy", the retry "trywhy", over a buffer "bufwhy", over a surface "srfwhy") goes to
  the kernel in pieces of 38 characters, "problem texwhy0 ...", "problem texwhy1 ...", up to 6 pieces, each reason once, at most 8 a
  process; native-adreno 0009 prints them as "GuampMetal: client <process>: problem texwhyK ...".
- Before the other fallbacks, the held surface imports (0010) are let go and the descriptor is tried again as asked
  ("native-metal: texture made after letting held imports go").
Applies after 0001, 0002, 0003, 0009, 0010 and 0011; the Objective-C++ is not compiled outside the CI.

